# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Infrastructure Release binaries — see infrastructure/README.md.
# The RAH-OIP Infrastructure Release engineering content (scripts,
# manifest, docs, checksums) IS tracked, under infrastructure/. Its
# binary payload is not: Docker image exports, the curated .deb
# package pool, and the packaged release archive are large,
# redistributable/regenerable content, kept physically present on
# disk for local build/test convenience but never committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tar
*.deb
*.zip
*.gz

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Packager-generated Application Release output and build artifacts —
# these are produced, not authored; regenerate them, don't commit them.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/dist/
**/build/
*_Release_*/
docker-images/*.tar

# Exception: the Platform's own Golden Release Fixtures under
# tests/fixtures/releases/ are deliberately authored, checked-in test
# data (same category as their release.yaml/checksums, already tracked)
# — not Packager output. Their docker-images/*.tar archives are small,
# real, working Docker images the PL6+ test suite genuinely needs on a
# fresh clone; the broad *.tar / docker-images/*.tar rules above were
# silently swallowing them (a real gap discovered building PL6 — the
# committed fixtures had a placeholder tar this whole time, working only
# because no test ever needed a fresh clone until now).
!tests/fixtures/releases/**/*.tar

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VM / Hyper-V artifacts — snapshots and exports never belong in Git,
# see docs/infrastructure-reference/golden-baseline.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.vhdx
*.vhd
*.vmcx
*.vmrs

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Credentials and local secrets — never committed. Real environment
# credentials live outside this repo entirely (see
# docs/infrastructure-reference/lab-environment-sanitized.md for what
# was intentionally left out and why).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
**/*credentials*
**/*LAB_ENVIRONMENT_REFERENCE*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Language/tooling ecosystem noise (Packager is Python, Platform is
# Python + a web frontend per Architecture V1).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
*.log
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editor/OS noise
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
